Under Section 482 the inherent jurisdiction of the court can be exercised (i) to give effect to an order under the Cr PC;
Tarun Bansal And Another vs State Of U.P. And Another on 7 June, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/36890191/
8 (ii) to prevent the abuse of the process of the court; and (iii) to otherwise secure the ends of justice.

Inherent power under Section 482 CrPC can be exercised:
(i) to give effect to an order under the Code;
(ii) to prevent abuse of the process of the Court, and (iii) to otherwise secure the ends of justice.
